[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two shallow, matte ceramic bowls set on an aged, weathered oak kitchen table. The bowls are placed side by side, with one in sharp focus in the immediate foreground and the second slightly blurred behind it. The camera angle is a 3/4 overhead view, roughly 40 degrees, ensuring every component in both bowls is clearly visible. Soft, natural side light spills from a window on the left, casting gentle, natural shadows and highlighting the texture of the sauce. Each bowl contains a base of steaming brown rice, topped with tender, golden-brown chicken breast chunks nestled next to vibrant green peas. The chicken and peas are coated in a thick, opaque, warm yellow-orange curry sauce, with the yogurt fully incorporated to create a smooth, creamy consistency. A generous scattering of fresh chopped cilantro sits atop the curry. Beside the bowls lies a slightly crumpled linen napkin and a single garlic clove, with a few stray grains of brown rice and a small fragment of cilantro scattered on the wood surface near the bowls. The scene displays realistic, lived-in imperfections: an asymmetric garnish placement, a tiny, natural sauce drip on the rim of the bowl, and a warm, inviting atmosphere. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating — lived-in, warm, authentic. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. The image should be indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a printed cookbook."
]
